# Design Docs Are the Source of Truth

Anything that must survive across chat sessions — data structures, protocols, formulas, decisions — lives in the design docs, not in chat history.

The layered docs and what belongs where:

| Doc | Owns |
|---|---|
| `docs/product.html` | Gameplay, core loops, what we deliberately don't build |
| `docs/tech-design.md` | Domain rules: credit formula, EV mapping, battle math, settlement |
| `docs/architecture.md` | Component selection, module boundaries, event contracts, sequences, repo layout |
| `docs/REVIEW.md` | Open decisions awaiting the user's ruling |
| `journal/WORKLOG.md` + `journal/TODO.md` | Session history and open work items (see session-journal rule) |

Working rules:

- **Read before you build.** Check the relevant doc section before implementing. If the implementation must deviate, update the doc in the same change — docs and code are never allowed to disagree.
- **Record on change.** Introducing or changing a data structure, event topic/schema, API, config namespace, or numeric formula → update the owning doc immediately, not "later".
- **Undecided goes to REVIEW.md.** A choice with real trade-offs becomes a review block (options + recommendation) instead of a silent decision buried in code.
- **Update over proliferate.** Extend the docs above; don't scatter design notes across new README/notes files.
